2,1,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Midori,,Hello everyone. I think we should look into who takes responsibility when things go wrong and how our plans evolve over time.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree we need stability. I am concerned about how new software will interact with our actual physical environment and the peak season.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,"I want to see if we're just buying things that will rot in five years or if we're paying for ""fixes"" that don't actually work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I am worried about the people. We need to know if the staff can actually handle another rollout without breaking.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A charming start. I'm personally fascinated by the ""invisible"" costs—those delightful little surprises that appear on invoices long after the champagne has been drunk.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, that's a good point. Maybe looking at the last outage or the cutover history would help us see where the gaps in ownership are?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,Yes. I want to see the depot calendar and the yard devices. We can't afford a system that crashes because it doesn't understand our hardware.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're speaking my language. But let's not just look at the cost; let's look at the upgrade history. I hate stagnant systems.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,I think we should check the administrator retirements and the depot supervisors' experiences. The human cost is often the highest risk.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, May. Though I suspect the ""upgrade history"" is often just a euphemism for ""additional fees."" I'll be digging into the financial trail.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,I'll focus on the support ownership during the outage and the warehouse rule changes. I want to see if the plan stayed aligned with the business.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'll stick with the depot calendar and the yard devices. The physical reality of the floor is where this project will succeed or fail.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,I'm going for the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move. Let's see how they handle migrations.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"I will look into administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as the depot supervisors and the last rollout.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests and the five years of renewal invoices. Let's see where the money actually goes.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
