30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems we have a pattern. Support is fragmented, and our initial plans are quickly outdated by new business needs. We need a vendor who offers a single point of accountability.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are worrying. Our hardware is outdated and our peak season is brutal. Any vendor that requires a ""freeze"" or modern hardware will fail us.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, it's just as I feared. We have a habit of letting systems age into fossils and paying outsiders to do ""lifts"" that leave a mess behind.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are thinner on people than we admit. The people holding things together are stretched too thin, and the crews struggle with retraining.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How predictable. The board loves a low entry price but ignores the bleeding from the operating budget. We are paying a ""convenience tax"" on fragmented licenses.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, if the hardware is the issue, maybe a hosted solution is better? But we must ensure the vendor takes full ownership of the uptime.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"A hosted solution is only a benefit if it works with the old scanners. If it requires a total hardware refresh, it's a non-starter for the budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. And if we go hosted, I don't want a ""black box"" where we can't update anything without paying a consultant to fix a broken migration.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"I'm less concerned about the box and more about the training. If the vendor doesn't provide on-site, hands-on support, the supervisors will just ignore the system.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A hosted solution often hides the cost in ""service fees"" that escalate. I'd prefer a fixed-price model over a ""flexible"" one that flexes only in the vendor's favor.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried that if we choose a rigid, fixed-price system, we'll be back in six months with a plan that doesn't match our business. We need a balance.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I don't care about ""flexibility"" if the system can't survive a December peak. I want a vendor that understands the grit of the depot floor.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward whoever has the best track record for clean migrations. I can't stand the thought of another ""2018 pay move"" disaster.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we can't hire new administrators, the vendor must be the administrator. We need a partner who does the heavy lifting, not just a software provider.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, ""partners"" are often the most expensive guests in the house. I want a contract where the total cost of ownership is capped and transparent.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
