58,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Meridian seems a bit too rigid with ""fixed configuration,"" but Corvus is exactly the fragmented mess we have now. I'm torn between Meridian and Anchor.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Anchor is the only one that puts engineers on-site. Given our hardware and the peak season, having people here to fix things in real-time is essential.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Anchor's on-site engineering is tempting, but ""on the company's own servers"" sounds like a recipe for another aging fossil. Tessera is too reliant on a ""partner firm.""","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I strongly prefer Anchor. With our administrator shortage, having their engineers here to support the crews and supervisors is the only way this lands safely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Corvus is a financial nightmare waiting to happen—modular licenses are where the hidden costs hide. Meridian's fixed configuration is a relief for the budget.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, but will Meridian's fixed configuration survive our business changes? @Ryuji, would Anchor's on-site team be able to handle the ownership of the whole system?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Yes. If they are on-site, they see the yard devices and the calendar. They can't ignore the reality of the floor when they are standing on it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm still worried about the ""own servers"" part of Anchor. But Tessera's ""partner firm"" for migration is exactly what caused the 2018 pay move mess.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the risk of a server crash is lower than the risk of the staff simply refusing to use a system they don't understand. Anchor's presence is key.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While I adore the predictability of Meridian, I can see the logic in Anchor. On-site engineers are a known cost, whereas ""cloud flexibility"" is often a blank check.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"If Anchor's engineers take ownership of the rollout and the stability, it solves my biggest fear. I can live with on-site servers if the accountability is clear.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It's the only choice. We cannot risk a remote support team trying to troubleshoot a 10-year-old scanner during the December rush.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I suppose I can tolerate the servers if it means we avoid the ""outsourced migration"" trap. Anchor's direct engineering approach is cleaner than a partner firm.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for Anchor. We cannot ask our remaining staff to carry the burden of a remote implementation. We need the boots on the ground.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the consensus is leaning toward the ""boots on the ground."" As long as the contract for those engineers is fixed and not an open-ended hourly bill.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Anchor provides the accountability and the direct support we need to ensure the system actually works for the people using it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed. It's the most cautious and reasonable path for our specific environment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine. I'll take the risk of the servers over the risk of a botched, outsourced data lift. Anchor it is.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm glad we agree. The staff will be much more likely to accept the change if they have direct help.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Very well. I shall cast my vote for Anchor, provided we keep a very tight leash on the ""additional services"" clause.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
